  "boundaries": [],
  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Meaning before action",
      "items": [
        "Problem → accepted intent → repository change → use → learning. A complete product path; a small trust kernel.",
        "Challenge examples; settle scope, assumptions, exceptions and guarantees. Accept / supersede / pending verification / reject. Only accepted meaning enters OpenSpec; compilation is not understanding.",
        "Accepted intent → transient Commitment; fresh Facts and applicable Attestations → bounded Plan and proof obligations. Source acceptance, delivery and Change completion are distinct. The same active Change keeps outstanding duties; archive after they settle. No-spec/archive changes retain proof identity.",
        "Subject + policy + intent + Facts + Plan are conjunctive. Only own PASS admits action; BLOCK / UNKNOWN cannot execute."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Independent work, selected objects",
      "items": [
        "Each worktree prepares and proves from its exact base. Fresh prewrite binds actor, lane and facts; a four-field Lease coordinates, never grants permission.",
        "Cooperate: compatible many or synthesis. Compete: zero or one. Explore: knowledge only, including negative results; all-drop integrates no code; retain useful findings if any.",
        "Prove the combined object; recheck; CAS the candidate ref; observe and attest. Candidate drift requires fresh combination checks before another attempt.",
        "Work authors; candidate integrates; proposal reviews; dev accepts; main releases. MR/PR or authorized maintainer selects the same object for separate accepted-root CAS. Retire proposal after dev acceptance and review closure, not main release."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Evidence and local effects",
      "items": [
        "Falsify exact candidates and combinations. Local / independent / hosted stay distinct. Independent per risk/policy; optional composite needs a responsible verifier and explicit rule. Evidence is not permission.",
        "Exact prestate → evaluate → own PASS → fresh recheck → apply once → post-observe → attest. One local linearization point; no global or cross-provider CAS.",
        "Attestation is the sole durable semantic result: predicate, bindings, validity, verifier; never permission. Commitment/Facts/Plan are transient. Experiments and change relations derive; no workflow ledger, compatibility residue or memory-backed truth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Native owners, open capabilities",
      "items": [
        "Source/tests/specs/docs/rules/Skills: one owner, current consumers, executable quality and bounded lifecycle. Profiles retain domain/layout/provider freedom; mutation requires verified OpenSpec. OpenSpec and Git are carriers, not semantic roots.",
        "People and replaceable agents compose Skills, generators, verifiers and native tools; prefer mature official capabilities. Names identify responsibilities; versions mark interpretation boundaries. Contracts bind I/O, identity, permission, cancellation and failure. Pure semantics, bounded effects; no capability grants authority.",
